**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Collection & Delivery**

| **Name** | **Text** | **Runtime** | **Goal Type** | **Relation** |
|----------|----------|-------------|---------------|--------------|
| **G1**: DeliverResources | Deliver requested resources from storage to destination | `;` (sequential) | Perform | AND |
| **G1.1**: CollectionPhase | Collect resources from storages | `#` (parallel – several storages can be visited by different robots) | Perform | AND |
| **G1.2**: DeliveryPhase | Deliver collected resources to destination | `#` (parallel – several checkpoints can be handled by different robots) | Perform | AND |
| **G1.1.1**: NavigateToStorage | Robot navigates to the storage location | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G1.1.2**: RequestResources | Robot sends a request message for the specified resources | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G1.1.3**: WaitForResources | Robot waits until resources are retrieved and ready for pickup | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G1.1.4**: LowBatteryCollection | Handle low battery during collection (10 %) – if battery <10 % robot recharges and assigns mission to another robot | `FALLBACK(AT4, AT5)` | Perform | AND |
| **G1.2.1**: NavigateToDestination | Robot navigates to the delivery destination | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G1.2.2**: DeliverResourcesAtDestination | Robot delivers resources to the specified location | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G1.2.3**: LowBatteryDelivery | Handle low battery during delivery (30 %) – if battery <30 % robot returns resource to a checkpoint and assigns remaining task to another robot | `FALLBACK(AT8, AT9)` | Perform | AND |
| **G1.2.4**: AlertHandling | Handle failure to return resource to a checkpoint – trigger alert and report to sector manager | `FALLBACK(AT9, AT11)` | Perform | AND |

---

### Task Model

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** |
|----------|----------|--------------|-------------|-----------------------|
| **AT1**: NavigateToStorage | Robot moves from current position to the storage location | AND | storage | 1 |
| **AT2**: SendRequest | Robot sends a message to the storage specifying required resources | AND | storage | 1 |
| **AT3**: WaitForResources | Robot waits until the storage confirms that resources are ready for pickup | AND | storage | 1 |
| **AT4**: CheckBatteryLowCollection | Robot checks battery level; if <10 % it will trigger a recharge | AND | storage | 1 |
| **AT5**: RechargeAndAssign | Robot returns to recharging station, recharges and assigns the mission to another robot | OR | recharging‑station | 1 |
| **AT6**: NavigateToDestination | Robot moves from current position to the delivery destination | AND | destination | 1 |
| **AT7**: DeliverResources | Robot physically transfers resources to the specified location | AND | destination | 1 |
| **AT8**: CheckBatteryLowDelivery | Robot checks battery level; if <30 % it will trigger a return to checkpoint | AND | destination | 1 |
| **AT9**: ReturnToCheckpoint | Robot returns the resource to an intermediate checkpoint | AND | checkpoint | 1 |
| **AT10**: AssignRemainingTask | Robot assigns remaining delivery task to another robot that knows the resource position | AND | checkpoint | 1 |
| **AT11**: TriggerAlertAndReport | Robot triggers an alert and sends a report to the sector manager | AND | checkpoint | 1 |

---

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 → G1.1, G1.2** [AND][;] (collection must finish before delivery starts)
- **G1.1 → G1.1.1, G1.1.2, G1.1.3, G1.1.4** [AND][#] (each sub‑goal can run in parallel when multiple robots are available)
- **G1.2 → G1.2.1, G1.2.2, G1.2.3, G1.2.4** [AND][#]
- **G1.1.4 → AT4, AT5** [AND][FALLBACK(AT4, AT5)] (if battery <10 % then recharge)
- **G1.2.3 → AT8, AT9** [AND][FALLBACK(AT8, AT9)] (if battery <30 % then return to checkpoint)
- **G1.2.4 → AT9, AT11** [AND][FALLBACK(AT9, AT11)] (if return to checkpoint fails → alert)

The tables above provide a complete goal–task hierarchy that captures the mission’s requirements while respecting the required runtime annotations, goal types, and logical relationships.
